  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint $:$ Let $\\log \\left(x+\\sqrt{1+x^2}\\right)=t \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{1+x^2}+x}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}} d x=d t}{x+\\sqrt{1+x^2}}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{d x}{\\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{x}^2}}=\\mathrm{dt} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{I}=\\int \\frac{\\log \\left(\\mathrm{x}+\\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{x}^2}\\right.}{\\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{x}^2}} \\mathrm{dx}=\\int \\mathrm{t} \\cdot \\mathrm{dt} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{I}=\\frac{\\mathrm{t}^2}{2}+\\mathrm{c}=\\frac{\\left[\\log \\left(\\mathrm{x}+\\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}^2+1}\\right]^2\\right.}{2}+\\mathrm{c} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{2}, \\mathrm{~g}(\\mathrm{x})=\\log _{\\mathrm{e}}\\left(\\mathrm{x}+\\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{x}^2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
